      "category": "Species",
      "status": "established",
      "era": "Present day",
      "summary": "Several unusual bioluminescent fungi co-occur with the region's Blacksilver Willows.",
      "body": "In humid nights, these fungi faintly illuminate decaying branches, roots and the litter beneath [[blacksilver|Blacksilver Willows]]. Their association is observed; direct mutualistic symbiosis is not yet established.\n\nWorking invented species names include **Silverveil Bonnet**, **Lantern Root**, and **Widow's Lantern**. Actual fungal classification, toxicity and biochemical specificity remain research questions.\n\nThe light can account for some stationary green glow but cannot account for accounts of traveling luminous orbs.",
