      "summary": "Wealthy gold-rich Spanish captain with an offshoot Habsburg royal lineage who founded Santa Aurelia in 1608 and fell profoundly in love with Inés.",
      "body": "The captain finances [[santa-aurelia|Puerto de Santa Aurelia]] in 1608 as a strategic maritime supply/trade venture, seeking commercial success and enduring dynastic legacy.\n\nHis exact proposed invented ancestry is as an additional, privately acknowledged son of Don John of Austria, making him a grandson of Charles V. This is **deliberate alternate-history genealogy**; the precise branch remains provisional.\n\nHe develops deep love for the local Indigenous people and falls deeply, mutually in love with [[ines|Inés]], daughter of a local chief. Their marriage is not principally a political bargain; its consequences nevertheless profoundly influence the colony.\n\nHis original [[flagship|flagship]] survives in the port as a heritage attraction.\n\nAlonso occasionally traveled to Spain with Sáweli; her personal [[saweli-spain-journals|Iberian travel journals]] describe those voyages from her perspective.\n\nIn 1638 Alonso built [[palacio|the Casa de las Asambleas]] as a romantic gift to Sáweli/Inés, inspired by her affection for Spanish courtly celebrations.\n\nThe otherwise rigorously practical captain's most extravagant personal decision was to spend an enormous fortune creating the monumental [[palacio|Spanish-stone Casa de las Asambleas]] for Sáweli, entirely out of proportion to the colony's practical needs.",
