      "body": "**Southbank High School's mascot is the Wolves**—an explicit correction to the discarded 'Millers' proposal. Their proposed colors are forest green, steel gray and white, with a proposed home field called the **Wolves' Den** and student cheering section **the Pack**.\n\nAthletics and school spirit are a major part of independent [[southbank|Southbank]]'s identity. The Wolves meet the [[wisps|Willowwick Wisps]] in the proposed **Milltown Classic** and the [[santa-aurelia-captains|Captains]] in the proposed **Harbor–Howl**. Differences in resources do not imply consistent losses, and some rivalry games may be nonleague due to enrollment. See [[valley-highschool-rivalries|Valley High School Rivalries]].\n\n**Football dynasty:** the Southbank Wolves have five fictional Oregon state title seasons: **1984, 1998, 2009, 2017, and 2021**. They are one of the state's feared historic small-town football programs, not a perennial underdog. Some years the more affluent [[wisps|Wisps]] or [[santa-aurelia-captains|Captains]] enter as underdogs against the Wolves.",
