      "summary": "The Valley Three are statewide football dynasties with 20 combined titles; Willowwick's Wisps won five straight from 2021 through 2025.",
      "body": "High school athletics—football, basketball, wrestling, soccer, volleyball, track, baseball/softball, and student bands—are major forces in Valle de Santa Aurelia's daily community identity.\n\nThe **[[wisps|Willowwick Wisps]]** and **[[santa-aurelia-captains|Santa Aurelia Captains]]** meet in the proposed **Lantern and Anchor Game**. The Wisps and **[[southbank-wolves|Southbank Wolves]]** meet in the proposed **Milltown Classic**. The Wolves and Captains meet in the proposed **Harbor–Howl**. Rivalry names and trophies remain working details; **Southbank Wolves is established**, not the old Millers nickname.\n\nAdditional coastal and mining township schools are to be created as those places are developed. Schools can compete in different Oregon classifications and meet in nonleague events. See `docs/28-high-school-sports-and-rivalries.md`.\n\n**The Valley Three:** three nearby statewide football powers have **20 combined state championships** in this alternate Oregon history: Willowwick Wisps (nine, with five consecutive titles in 2021–2025), Santa Aurelia Captains (six), and Southbank Wolves (five). The programs' fictional title years are documented in `docs/28-high-school-sports-and-rivalries.md`. They dominate local attention and attract statewide scouting, media and visiting supporters. Their current divisions may differ (working alignment: Willowwick and Santa Aurelia 5A, Southbank 4A), so not every traditional rivalry game must be a league contest. No 2026 state title has yet been assigned.\n\n**Current hierarchy:** although all three programs are historic Oregon powerhouses, the [[wisps|Willowwick Wisps]] are the dominant recent dynasty, entering 2026 after **five straight state titles**. The Captains and Wolves are determined to end that streak. The Wolves' 2021 title belongs to a separate classification in the working alignment.",
