      "era": "Geographic planning v1 (2026)",
      "summary": "A multi-watershed 1,800-square-mile study region around the Columbia estuary, with proposed coordinates for all major cities, sacred forests, coastal communities and port infrastructure.",
      "body": "The historic **[[valle|Valle de Santa Aurelia]]** is a **roughly 1,800-square-mile** multi-watershed cultural region spanning the Columbia estuary, northern Pacific coast, Youngs River corridor, foothills and Coast Range uplands. The study polygon has **approximately 1,863 sq mi** under a local planar approximation, with approximately **70-mile east–west by 45-mile north–south** maximum extents; those are **planning envelopes, not surveyed limits**.\n\n**[[santa-aurelia|Santa Aurelia]]** (46.1880, -123.8313) uses Astoria's geographic site. **[[willowwick|Willowwick Grove]]** (46.0100, -123.6650) is placed in the modified upper Youngs River corridor. **[[southbank|Southbank]]** (46.0650, -123.7380) is a separate middle-valley township. The [[blackwood|Blackwood Ridge]] and [[witchwood|Witches' Wood]] are farther south, with [[reservation|sovereign tribal territory]] on their northwestern side and [[fernhollow|Fernhollow]] to the southwest; [[alderwood|Alderwood Lake]] lies in an eastern upland basin.\n\nPorts, outer coast, cruise terminal and [[coast-guard-base|joint Navy–Coast Guard base]] have separate proposed reference points. Real watersheds and river navigability must be respected; the cratonic geology and Alderwood Lake are fictional modifications needing terrain work. Full proposed coordinates, distances and design assumptions: `docs/29-geographic-master-plan.md`; machine-readable polygon and 20 points: `atlas/geography.geojson`.\n\nFour proposed natural-history coordinates now supplement the geo-registry: [[black-steps|Black Steps]] (45.950, -123.980), [[high-gorge|High Gorge]] (45.970, -123.590), [[blackwood-ravines|Blackwood Ravines]] (45.918, -123.655), and [[moor-ridges|Open Moor Ridges]] (45.910, -123.704). All require geology, rivers, elevation and ecological verification.\n\nThe GeoJSON registry now includes [[duskwood|Duskwood Township]] at a provisional center of **45.8750, -123.5920** on the forest's eastern/southeastern outskirts.",
