      "category": "Settlement",
      "status": "established",
      "era": "Present day; founding date working",
      "summary": "A small independent forest-edge township on the eastern outskirts of Witches' Wood, known for practical woodland life, old logging history and cautious respect for the ancient forest.",
      "body": "**Duskwood Township** is a small, independent year-round town on the **eastern/southeastern outskirts of [[witchwood|Witches' Wood]]** in [[blackwood|Blackwood Ridge]]. Its proposed center lies at **45.8750° N, 123.5920° W**, away from the ancient forest's central monuments and distinct from southwestern [[fernhollow|Fernhollow Country]] and northwestern [[reservation|sovereign reservation lands]]. Exact town boundaries, route geometry and streams await map validation.\n\nIt has a modest main street, homes and farms, small shops, repair trades, woodland service businesses, and families with generations of local knowledge. Working population **900–1,400**, not yet fixed. A proposed late-nineteenth-century crossroads/logging-service origin fits its surviving old grades and stories of failed forest exploitation, but the town is not itself cursed or abandoned. Residents forage on suitable permitted outer trails and often hear the native [[blackwood-echojay|Echojay]]. Some support legal conservation; others debate access and livelihoods. The active formal-protection campaign remains led by Fernhollow and tribal government, which retain separate authority.\n\nDuskwood is **not an extension of Fernhollow ecovillage**, not a new school in the established three-team rivalry, and not a public route through sacred sites. Its institutions, schools, named people, population and founding date remain open. More: `docs/35-duskwood-township.md` and [[geographic-master-plan|the regional geographic master plan]].\n\nFarms and horse properties on appropriate outer lands link Duskwood to [[valley-agriculture|regional agriculture]], youth [[valley-4h|4-H]] and [[valley-rodeo|rodeo]].",
